
📊 Retail Customer Behavior & RFM Analysis 

🚀 Project Overview
This project analyzes retail customer purchasing behavior using the RFM (Recency, Frequency, Monetary) framework to segment customers based on their engagement and spending patterns.
The objective is to help businesses identify:
High-value customers
Loyal customers
Customers at risk of churn
Inactive customers
The project is implemented using PySpark (Big Data Processing) and visualized using Power BI Dashboard


🎯 Business Objective

In retail and e-commerce businesses, understanding customer behavior is critical for:
Improving customer retention
Increasing revenue
Reducing churn
Running targeted marketing campaigns
RFM analysis helps convert raw transactional data into actionable business insights.



🛠️ Tech Stack

PySpark
Spark SQL
Pandas
Power BI
Retail Transaction Dataset (CSV)


📂 Project Workflow

1️⃣ Data Cleaning
Filtered dataset to remove:
Negative Quantity (returns)
Invalid Unit Price
Null Customer IDs


2️⃣ Feature Engineering

Created Total Revenue column:
Quantity * UnitPrice AS Total_Amount


3️⃣ RFM Calculation

Using Spark SQL:
Recency → Days since last purchase
Frequency → Number of transactions
Monetary → Total amount spent


4️⃣ RFM Scoring (Window Functions)

Each customer receives a score from 1–5 for each metric.

5️⃣ Customer Segmentation Logic


📊 Dashboard Insights
🔹 Total Customers: 4,338
🔹 Key Findings:

Champions → Highest revenue & most frequent buyers
Loyal Customers → Consistent repeat buyers
At Risk → High past engagement but declining activity
Hibernating → Low activity & low spenders

The dashboard provides:
Average Spending by Segment
Average Purchase Frequency by Segment
Customer Distribution Pie Chart
Total Customer Count KPI



📈 Business Impact

This segmentation enables businesses to:
Offer premium loyalty programs to Champions
Send retention campaigns to At-Risk customers
Run reactivation campaigns for Hibernating customers
Optimize marketing ROI
Improve revenue forecasting



📁 Output

Generated file:
rfm_customer_segments.csv

Columns include:

CustomerID
Recency
Frequency
Monetary
R_Score
F_Score
M_Score
Customer_Segment


